.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt NFDUMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nfdump
.Nd stable, read-only C ABI for nffile flow files
.Sh LIBRARY
The
.Nm libnfdump
library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nfdump.h
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef struct {
        uint32_t    abi_version;
        uint32_t    struct_size;
        const char *passphrase;
} nfdump_reader_options_t;
.Ed
.Pp
.Ft uint32_t
.Fn nfdump_abi_version void
.Ft nfdump_status_t
.Fn nfdump_reader_open "const char *path" "const nfdump_reader_options_t *options" "nfdump_reader_t **out_reader"
.Ft void
.Fn nfdump_reader_close "nfdump_reader_t *reader"
.Ft const char *
.Fn nfdump_reader_last_error "const nfdump_reader_t *reader"
.Ft nfdump_status_t
.Fn nfdump_reader_next "nfdump_reader_t *reader" "nfdump_record_view_t *record"
.Ft nfdump_status_t
.Fn nfdump_reader_file_info "const nfdump_reader_t *reader" "nfdump_file_info_t *out"
.Ft size_t
.Fn nfdump_field_count void
.Ft nfdump_status_t
.Fn nfdump_field_describe "nfdump_field_id_t field" "nfdump_field_info_t *out"
.Ft nfdump_status_t
.Fn nfdump_record_get "nfdump_reader_t *reader" "nfdump_field_id_t field" "void *out" "size_t out_size"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library is nfdump's small, stable public read ABI.
It opens nfdump nffile flow-capture files and exposes their records without
exposing nfdump's internal data structures or query engine.
It is intended for independently built C applications and language bindings.
The ABI is read-only: it contains no functions to modify, create, or write
flow files.
.Pp
The primary file format is nffile V3.
The current implementation also reads legacy nffile V2 input through
nfdump's in-memory conversion path.
Applications must not depend on that conversion for writing or on any
internal V2/V3 structure layout.
.Pp
Link with
.Fl lnfdump .
When installed with pkg-config metadata, a typical build is:
.Pp
.Dl cc $(pkg-config --cflags nfdump) reader.c -o reader $(pkg-config --libs nfdump)
.Sh ABI CONTRACT
The public header has no nfdump-internal header dependencies and may be used
by FFI generators.
.Vt nfdump_reader_t
is opaque; callers must allocate no reader object themselves and must access
it only through these functions.
.Pp
.Dv NFDUMP_ABI_VERSION
is the compile-time ABI version.
.Fn nfdump_abi_version
returns the ABI version of the loaded library, allowing dynamic callers to
check it before using the API.
.Pp
The public field identifiers are append-only ABI values.
They are deliberately independent from nfdump's internal extension IDs,
which are not public and can change with the file format.
Do not renumber, reuse, or derive meanings from the numeric values of
.Vt nfdump_field_id_t .
.Pp
Set both
.Va abi_version
and
.Va struct_size
when passing
.Vt nfdump_reader_options_t
to
.Fn nfdump_reader_open .
For
.Vt nfdump_file_info_t
and
.Vt nfdump_field_info_t ,
set only
.Va struct_size ;
the library fills
.Va abi_version
and the remaining result fields.
Future ABI versions can append members while retaining this convention.
.Sh READER LIFETIME
.Fn nfdump_reader_open
opens
.Fa path
read-only and, on success, stores a new reader in
.Fa *out_reader .
Pass a null
.Fa options
pointer for default options, or a properly initialized
.Vt nfdump_reader_options_t .
Its
.Va passphrase
member is null or an empty string for unencrypted files.
For encrypted files it supplies the passphrase; a missing or invalid
passphrase fails without a terminal prompt or stdin read.
.Pp
On any failed open,
.Fa *out_reader
is null and must not be closed.
.Fn nfdump_reader_close
releases a reader and accepts a null pointer.
.Pp
Call
.Fn nfdump_reader_next
to advance through the file.
On
.Dv NFDUMP_OK ,
it fills a
.Vt nfdump_record_view_t
with a one-based traversal
.Va ordinal ,
the raw record
.Va data ,
and its
.Va size .
The raw data is an opaque internal V4 record representation.
It is supplied only for pass-through or archival purposes; applications must
use
.Fn nfdump_record_get
to read fields and must not parse the raw bytes.
.Pp
The record view and its data are borrowed.
They remain valid only until the next
.Fn nfdump_reader_next
or
.Fn nfdump_reader_close
call on that reader.
Copy data which must survive either call.
.Pp
After a successful
.Fn nfdump_reader_next ,
.Fn nfdump_record_get
may read fields from the current record.
It copies the requested value into
.Fa out .
The caller supplies an output buffer at least as large as the field's
published size; otherwise it returns
.Dv NFDUMP_ERR_INVALID_ARG .
If a valid field is not present in a particular record,
.Dv NFDUMP_ABSENT
is returned and the output buffer is left unchanged.
.Pp
.Fn nfdump_reader_file_info
returns file statistics and time bounds immediately after a successful open.
The returned
.Va ident
string is borrowed and remains valid until the reader is closed; it may be
null.
.Fn nfdump_reader_last_error
returns a non-null, NUL-terminated diagnostic string for the most recent
iteration or field-access error on that reader.
It is empty if no such error has occurred.
Open errors have no reader and are reported through nfdump's normal logging.
.Sh FIELDS AND BYTE ORDER
.Fn nfdump_field_count
returns the number of valid public field IDs.
Values from 1 through that count can be described with
.Fn nfdump_field_describe .
The latter provides a stable field name, type, and output size for generic
or introspecting consumers.
.Pp
The available field types are
.Dv NFDUMP_T_U8 ,
.Dv NFDUMP_T_U16 ,
.Dv NFDUMP_T_U32 ,
.Dv NFDUMP_T_U64 ,
and
.Dv NFDUMP_T_IPV6 .
All scalar values are copied in host byte order.
The two address fields,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_SRC_ADDR
and
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_DST_ADDR ,
are the exception: each is a 16-byte IPv6 buffer in network byte order.
IPv4 addresses use the IPv4-mapped IPv6 form specified by RFC 4291
.Po
.Dq ::ffff:a.b.c.d
.Pc .
.Pp
The current stable field set covers:
.Bl -tag -width "routing and classification"
.It timestamps
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_FIRST_SEEN ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_LAST_SEEN ,
and
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_RECEIVED
in milliseconds since the Unix epoch.
.It network tuple and protocol
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_IP_VERSION ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_SRC_ADDR ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_DST_ADDR ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_SRC_PORT ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_DST_PORT ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_ICMP_TYPE ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_ICMP_CODE ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_PROTO ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_TCP_FLAGS ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_SRC_TOS ,
and
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_FWD_STATUS .
.It counters and aggregation
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_IN_PACKETS ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_IN_BYTES ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_OUT_PACKETS ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_OUT_BYTES ,
and
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_AGGR_FLOWS .
Reverse-direction counters can be absent.
.It routing and classification
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_INPUT_IF ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_OUTPUT_IF ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_SRC_AS ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_DST_AS ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_SRC_VLAN ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_DST_VLAN ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_SRC_MASK ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_DST_MASK ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_DIRECTION ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_DST_TOS ,
and
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_FLOW_END_REASON .
.It exporter metadata
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_EXPORTER_ID ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_ENGINE_TYPE ,
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_ENGINE_ID ,
and
.Dv NFDUMP_FIELD_NF_VERSION .
.El
.Pp
The installed
.In nfdump.h
is authoritative for the enum's exact field list and types.
New fields may be appended in later ABI-compatible releases.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Vt nfdump_status_t
return one of the following values.
.Bl -tag -width "NFDUMP_ERR_UNSUPPORTED"
.It Dv NFDUMP_OK
The operation succeeded.
.It Dv NFDUMP_EOF
.Fn nfdump_reader_next
reached the end of the flow records.
.It Dv NFDUMP_ABSENT
The requested field is not available on the current record.
.It Dv NFDUMP_ERR_IO
An allocation or other resource failure occurred.
.It Dv NFDUMP_ERR_FORMAT
The file could not be opened, validated, or decoded; this includes corrupt,
truncated, unrecognized, and unreadable flow data.
.It Dv NFDUMP_ERR_UNSUPPORTED
The file layout is newer than this library, or a requested feature is not
compiled into this build.
.It Dv NFDUMP_ERR_CRYPTO
The supplied crypto context could not be prepared, for example because crypto
support is not available in this build.
.It Dv NFDUMP_ERR_INVALID_ARG
An argument is null or out of range, an ABI structure is too small, there is
no current record, or an output buffer is too small.
.El
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Do not concurrently use one
.Vt nfdump_reader_t
from multiple threads.
Independent readers are safe to use concurrently.
.Fn nfdump_reader_open
briefly serializes on a single process-wide lock for every call, not only
for encrypted files, held for the duration of the underlying file
validation step; this keeps key derivation for encrypted files race-free
without a per-file lock.
It does not affect
.Fn nfdump_reader_next ,
.Fn nfdump_record_get ,
or any other call on an already-open reader, none of which take a lock.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <nfdump.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdio.h>
int
main(int argc, char **argv)
{
        nfdump_reader_options_t options = {
                .abi_version = NFDUMP_ABI_VERSION,
                .struct_size = sizeof(options),
        };
        nfdump_reader_t *reader = NULL;
        nfdump_status_t status;

        if (argc != 2 ||
            nfdump_reader_open(argv[1], &options, &reader) != NFDUMP_OK)
                return 1;

        nfdump_record_view_t record;
        while ((status = nfdump_reader_next(reader, &record)) == NFDUMP_OK) {
                uint64_t bytes;
                if (nfdump_record_get(reader, NFDUMP_FIELD_IN_BYTES,
                    &bytes, sizeof(bytes)) == NFDUMP_OK)
                        printf("%llu: %llu bytes\en",
                            (unsigned long long)record.ordinal,
                            (unsigned long long)bytes);
        }
        nfdump_reader_close(reader);
        return status == NFDUMP_EOF ? 0 : 1;
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nfcapd 1 ,
.Xr nfdump 1 ,
.Xr nfpcapd 1 ,
.Xr sfcapd 1
.Sh HISTORY
The public
.Nm
read ABI first appeared in nfdump 1.8.
